    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0546" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.51632 National City Bank/7: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-05T17:00:00-05:00">March 5, 1930—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Does your No. 7, March 4, 5 p.m. mean that it is not possible to put up a bond
                    instead of depositing securities or cash? The bank is <pb facs="0547" n="467"
                        xml:id="pg467"/> very anxious to exhaust all possibilities along this line.
                    Please reply by cable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
